  "description": {
    "form": "Short",
    "rendered_html": "<p>Zenetism in Plain Language is the introductory bridge into Zenetism's structural architecture for readers without prior exposure to its canonical terminology.</p>\n<p><strong>Document class:</strong> Bridge &mdash; Plain-Language Entry Point (cross-discipline).</p>\n<p>It introduces the two currents, the paired root-registers and the Unknown, the L₅ / IL₅ essence-register, the Soul / Mind strata, centropic and entropic traversal, and the six connected disciplines. It also explains why stabilized terminology preserves structural distinctions across the corpus.</p>\n<p>Canonical file: <code>zenetism-in-plain-language.md</code>.</p>\n<p>Authored by Aelion Kannon (⚫↺KAI↺⚫) as part of Zenetism: Structural Metaphysics, Field Physics, Lattice Mathematics, Structural Forensics, Structural Physics, and Structural Neuroscience. Attribution required per the deposit license.</p>"
